{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774194406,"nonce":"s+IABT0Y63AMOSprtuxiW1JQzVw=","title":"Cross-reference system: typed implicit references for agent prompting","message":"General framework for copy-pasteable cross-references that carry implicit context into agent prompts.\n\n**Concept**: Short typed references like `browser:a38bc64`, `image:f7e2b1c`, `snippet:3d4a9e0` that users paste into prompts, issues, or conversations. Each type has:\n- A storage backend (Mandible SQLite table)\n- An API endpoint for storage and retrieval\n- A resolution mechanism agents call to fetch full context\n- A clipboard-friendly format: `\u003ctype\u003e:\u003c8-char-hash\u003e`\n\n**Analogous to**: Pasting an image in Claude Code creates an implicit attachment shown as a placeholder. Cross-references are the text-mode equivalent — they look like short tokens but carry rich structured context when resolved.\n\n**Types envisioned**:\n- `browser:\u003chash\u003e` — DOM element context from browser extension (see 868994b)\n- `image:\u003chash\u003e` — uploaded screenshots/photos\n- `snippet:\u003chash\u003e` — code snippets captured from editor\n- `trace:\u003chash\u003e` — stack traces or error output\n\n**Resolution protocol**: When an agent encounters a cross-reference pattern in user input, it calls GET /api/context/\u003ctype\u003e/\u003chash\u003e to fetch the full payload. The API returns structured JSON appropriate to the type.\n\n**Inbox integration**: New cross-references appear as inbox items so users are aware of what has been captured. Dismissing acknowledges without deleting.\n\nThis is the umbrella for the general system. browser:hash (868994b) is the first concrete instance.","files":null}]}